      "images": [],
      "reading_time_minutes": 1,
      "severity": "medium",
      "summary": "Overview A privilege escalation vulnerability exists in the tdeio64.sys driver due to an unprotected input/output control (IOCTL) dispatch routine that fails to validate the origin and permissions of user-supplied requests. An unprivileged local attacker can abuse exposed IOCTL dispatch routines [RM1.1][MB1.2]to perform arbitrary kernel memory read and write operations, ultimately obtaining NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM privileges and compromising the security of the affected system. Description The tdeio",
